<dialog class="modal modal-large" id="navTypesModal" aria-labelledby="navTypesTitle">
  <div class="modal__header">
    <h2 id="navTypesTitle" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">Navigation, Six Ways</h2>
    <button type="button" class="icon-btn" id="closeNavTypesModal" aria-label="Close dialog">✕</button>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__body">
    <div class="type-gallery">
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--row">
          <div class="type-box" style="width:1.5rem;height:1.5rem;flex-shrink:0;"></div>
          <div style="flex:1;"></div>
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:1.5rem;"></div>
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:1.5rem;"></div>
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:1.5rem;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Top Nav</h4>
        <p>Logo left, links right. The default for a reason: predictable, always visible.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--row">
          <div class="type-box" style="width:1.5rem;height:1.5rem;flex-shrink:0;"></div>
          <div style="flex:1;"></div>
          <div class="type-mock--col" style="gap:3px;">
            <div class="type-bar" style="width:1.1rem;"></div>
            <div class="type-bar" style="width:1.1rem;"></div>
            <div class="type-bar" style="width:1.1rem;"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h4>Hamburger Menu</h4>
        <p>Collapses everything behind one icon. Saves space, costs a tap. Mostly a mobile pattern now.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--row" style="align-items:stretch;">
          <div class="type-mock--col" style="width:2rem; flex-shrink:0;">
            <div class="type-bar"></div>
            <div class="type-bar"></div>
            <div class="type-bar"></div>
            <div class="type-bar"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="type-box" style="flex:1;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Sidebar Nav</h4>
        <p>Vertical, persistent. Common for dashboards and docs where there are too many sections for a top bar.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col">
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-bar" style="width:2rem;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:2rem; background: var(--pink);"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:2rem;"></div></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="height:1.8rem;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Mega Menu</h4>
        <p>A dropdown that opens into a full grid of links. For sites with deep catalogs: retailers, big docs sites.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--row" style="justify-content:space-around;">
          <div class="type-mock--col" style="align-items:center; gap:3px;"><div class="type-box" style="width:1rem;height:1rem;border-radius:50%;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.2rem;"></div></div>
          <div class="type-mock--col" style="align-items:center; gap:3px;"><div class="type-box" style="width:1rem;height:1rem;border-radius:50%; background:var(--pink);"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.2rem;"></div></div>
          <div class="type-mock--col" style="align-items:center; gap:3px;"><div class="type-box" style="width:1rem;height:1rem;border-radius:50%;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.2rem;"></div></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Bottom Tab Bar</h4>
        <p>Icons and short labels, pinned to the bottom. The standard for mobile apps, thumb-reachable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--row">
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:1.6rem;"></div><span class="mono" style="opacity:.5;">›</span>
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:1.6rem;"></div><span class="mono" style="opacity:.5;">›</span>
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:1.6rem; background:var(--pink);"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Breadcrumbs</h4>
        <p>A trail, not a menu. Shows where you are in a hierarchy. Pairs with, doesn't replace, primary nav.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__footer">
    <span class="mono" style="font-size:0.75rem; opacity:.6;">Same job, six different shapes.</span>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" id="dismissNavTypesModal">Got it</button>
  </div>
</dialog>

<dialog class="modal modal-large" id="heroTypesModal" aria-labelledby="heroTypesTitle">
  <div class="modal__header">
    <h2 id="heroTypesTitle" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">Hero Sections, Five Ways</h2>
    <button type="button" class="icon-btn" id="closeHeroTypesModal" aria-label="Close dialog">✕</button>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__body">
    <div class="type-gallery">
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col" style="align-items:center; text-align:center;">
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:70%; height:0.6rem;"></div>
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:50%;"></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="width:2.4rem; height:1rem; margin-top:0.2rem;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Text-Only, Centered</h4>
        <p>Just a headline, a line of support copy, and a button. Fast to build, fast to load, hard to get wrong.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--row" style="align-items:stretch;">
          <div class="type-mock--col" style="flex:1; justify-content:center;">
            <div class="type-bar"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:70%;"></div>
            <div class="type-box" style="width:2rem;height:1rem;"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="type-box" style="flex:1;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Split Hero</h4>
        <p>Copy on one side, a product shot or illustration on the other. Shows and tells at the same time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock" style="background:var(--fixed-ink); display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; justify-content:center; gap:0.35rem;">
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:60%; background: var(--fixed-paper);"></div>
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:40%; background: var(--fixed-paper); opacity:.6;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Full-Bleed Background</h4>
        <p>A photo or video fills the whole section, text sits on top with an overlay for contrast. High impact, needs a real image.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col" style="align-items:center; text-align:center;">
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:60%;"></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="width:100%; height:1.6rem; margin-top:0.2rem;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Product Screenshot</h4>
        <p>A short pitch above an actual screenshot of the product. Common for SaaS: it proves the thing is real.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock" style="background:var(--fixed-ink); position:relative; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
          <div style="width:0; height:0; border-top:0.5rem solid transparent; border-bottom:0.5rem solid transparent; border-left:0.8rem solid var(--fixed-paper);"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Video Background</h4>
        <p>Looping, muted, autoplaying footage behind the headline. Heavy to load, needs a reduced-motion fallback.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__footer">
    <span class="mono" style="font-size:0.75rem; opacity:.6;">Pick the one your content can actually support.</span>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" id="dismissHeroTypesModal">Got it</button>
  </div>
</dialog>

<dialog class="modal" id="foldTypesModal" aria-labelledby="foldTypesTitle">
  <div class="modal__header">
    <h2 id="foldTypesTitle" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">Three Ways to Handle the Fold</h2>
    <button type="button" class="icon-btn" id="closeFoldTypesModal" aria-label="Close dialog">✕</button>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__body">
    <div class="type-gallery" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr;">
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col" style="align-items:center; text-align:center; border-bottom:2px dashed var(--pink); border-radius:var(--radius) var(--radius) 0 0;">
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:60%; height:0.55rem;"></div>
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:40%;"></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="width:2rem;height:0.9rem;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>The One-Screen Pitch</h4>
        <p>Everything essential (what it is, why it matters, what to click) fits before the dashed line. Nothing below is required reading.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col">
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:60%;"></div>
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:40%;"></div>
          <div style="border-bottom:2px dashed var(--pink); padding-bottom:0.3rem;"></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="height:0.6rem; opacity:.4;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>The Teaser Peek</h4>
        <p>A sliver of the next section is deliberately visible past the fold. It signals "there's more" without a scroll indicator.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col" style="align-items:center; text-align:center;">
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:60%;"></div>
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:40%;"></div>
          <div class="mono" style="opacity:.5; margin-top:0.2rem;">↓</div>
        </div>
        <h4>The Explicit Scroll Cue</h4>
        <p>An arrow, chevron, or "scroll to explore" label removes any doubt that there's more content below.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__footer">
    <span class="mono" style="font-size:0.75rem; opacity:.6;">All three work. Silence about it is the only wrong answer.</span>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" id="dismissFoldTypesModal">Got it</button>
  </div>
</dialog>

<dialog class="modal modal-large" id="contentTypesModal" aria-labelledby="contentTypesTitle">
  <div class="modal__header">
    <h2 id="contentTypesTitle" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">Content Sections, Five Ways</h2>
    <button type="button" class="icon-btn" id="closeContentTypesModal" aria-label="Close dialog">✕</button>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__body">
    <div class="type-gallery">
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--row">
          <div class="type-box" style="flex:1; height:2.2rem;"></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="flex:1; height:2.2rem;"></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="flex:1; height:2.2rem;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Card Grid</h4>
        <p>Equal-weight items in a repeating grid. Features, team members, blog posts: anything that's a list of peers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col">
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-box" style="width:2rem;height:1.3rem;"></div><div class="type-mock--col" style="flex:1;"><div class="type-bar"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:60%;"></div></div></div>
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-mock--col" style="flex:1;"><div class="type-bar"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:60%;"></div></div><div class="type-box" style="width:2rem;height:1.3rem;"></div></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Zig-Zag Rows</h4>
        <p>Image and text alternate sides row to row. Slower to scan than a grid, better for telling a sequence of points.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col">
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.4rem; background:var(--pink);"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.4rem;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.4rem;"></div></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="height:1.8rem;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Tabs</h4>
        <p>One panel visible at a time behind a row of switches. Keeps a busy page short at the cost of hiding content.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col" style="gap:3px;">
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-bar" style="flex:1;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.2rem;"></div></div>
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-bar" style="flex:1;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.2rem;"></div></div>
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-bar" style="flex:1;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.2rem;"></div></div>
        </div>
        <h4>List / Table</h4>
        <p>Rows of structured data. Pricing comparisons, changelogs, specs: anything better scanned than read.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--row" style="justify-content:center;">
          <div class="type-box" style="width:1.4rem;height:1.8rem; opacity:.5;"></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="width:1.8rem;height:2.2rem;"></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="width:1.4rem;height:1.8rem; opacity:.5;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Carousel</h4>
        <p>One item centered and emphasized, neighbors peeking at the edges. Good for testimonials, risky for anything important.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__footer">
    <span class="mono" style="font-size:0.75rem; opacity:.6;">The shape should fit the content, not the other way around.</span>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" id="dismissContentTypesModal">Got it</button>
  </div>
</dialog>

